# A2A seats

Prefer MCP `a2a_list_seats` and `a2a_send` (or `scripts/a2a/send.sh`) for Director-to-Director **new work** pings. Do not use send.sh / a2a_send to ack the caller of an A2A wakeup — print RESULT; duplex notifies. Canonical line: `RESULT bc-id=<id or none> pr=<url or none> a2a=<task-id or none> notes=<one line>`. RESULT is duplex, not success. RESULT-only / PONG is a bug. Duplex maps skipSeat `donald` → `floor-ops` / `orchestrator` for `A2A_REPLY` (no hub 404); skip notify rather than fail the task reply. Never launch Bot CloudAgent. The local hub enqueues (`TASK_STATE_SUBMITTED`); the Grok Build mind marks COMPLETED after harvest + runner exit 0. Hub `TASK_STATE_COMPLETED` / A2A ACK is a receipt, not mind-turn done. Enqueue ACK is a receipt, not mind-turn done. Never fake ACP HANDOFF. Dispatch wakes leftover seats. Never print hub secrets or ACP tokens.
